# Build context hygiene for both Dockerfiles in this directory.
#
# Dockerfile does `COPY . /app/`, so anything left in this directory ends up in
# the image. Only source belongs there: credentials, runtime state, the Owlet
# app and the proprietary libraries must never be baked in.
#
# Docker semantics (not .gitignore): a pattern is matched against the path from
# the context root, so `*.env` would only match at the top level. File patterns
# below use `**/` to match at any depth; a matching directory excludes its
# whole contents.

# Tests and caches
tests/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.venv*/
**/venv/

# Credentials: compose .env files, owlet.env, keys and certificates
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.env
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.crt
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/secrets/
**/ssl/
# JSON is never source here; at runtime it is secrets (ui.json, go2rtc.json,
# login-guard.json) or per-camera state.
**/*.json
docker-compose.override.yml
compose.override.yml

# Runtime state that belongs in the /config volume, not the image
**/config/
**/owlet.yaml
**/*.gen.yaml
**/cameras/
**/uploads/
**/*.log

# The Owlet app and its unpacked bundle (proprietary; supplied by the user)
**/*.apk
**/*.apkm
**/*.xapk
**/*.apks
**/bundle/

# Proprietary TUTK libraries are mounted at /app/libs, never baked into an image.
**/*.so

# Local captures and scratch files
**/frame*.png
**/*.scratch
**/captures/
**/mitm-data/
**/frida-server-*
